.TH ceff "1" "Crane Commands" "2025" "ceff Manual"

.SH "NAME"
.LP
ceff \- Display real-time status during job execution.

.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.LP
ceff [\fIoptions\fP]

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.LP
ceff displays real-time status information during job execution, providing dynamic metrics for jobs running in the cluster. 
It shows up-to-date information on job status, resource utilization, and efficiency metrics, helping users monitor job performance and resource consumption.

.SH "OPTIONS"
.LP

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.PD
Display help information and exit.
.IP

.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR <\fIstring\fR>
.PD
Configuration file path (default: "/etc/crane/config.yaml").
.IP

.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
.PD
Output task information in JSON format as returned by the backend (for programmatic use).
.IP

.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
.PD
Display the version of ceff and exit.
.IP

.SH "MAIN OUTPUT ITEMS"
.LP
Key fields displayed when querying job status:

.TP
\fBJobId\fR
Job unique identifier.
.IP

.TP
\fBQos\fR
Cluster name where the job is running.
.IP

.TP
\fBUser/Group\fR
User and user group who submitted the job.
.IP

.TP
\fBAccount\fR
Account name associated with the job.
.IP

.TP
\fBState\fR
Current job status (e.g., COMPLETED, FAILED, CANCELLED, etc.).
.IP

.TP
\fBCores\fR
Number of CPU cores used by the job.
.IP

.TP
\fBNodes\fR
Number of nodes allocated to the job.
.IP

.TP
\fBCores per node\fR
Number of cores allocated to each node.
.IP

.TP
\fBCPU Utilized\fR
Actual CPU time used by the job.
.IP

.TP
\fBCPU Efficiency\fR
CPU usage efficiency, expressed as the percentage of actual CPU time used relative to the allocated core wall time.
.IP

.TP
\fBJob Wall-clock time\fR
Total elapsed time from job start to end.
.IP

.TP
\fBMemory Utilized\fR
Actual memory amount used by the job.
.IP

.TP
\fBMemory Efficiency\fR
Memory usage efficiency, expressed as the percentage of actual memory used relative to the allocated memory.
.IP


.SH "SEE ALSO"
.LP
\fBcacct\fR(1), \fBcqueue\fR(1), \fBcrun\fR(1)